The tick looks at the units only once the count is past the release.
A thread whose account reached a tick would wait a tick longer on the spent queue;
the release lies ahead of the count.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test smp-test qemu-replay
Report: a thread waits on another queue than its account says
Report: the release is for a tick already past

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -496,7 +496,7 @@ static void tick_advance(uint32_t ticks)
     nearest_deadline = nearest;
     for (uint32_t c = 0; c < CORES; c++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(CORES);
-        if (!tick_before(sched_ticks, cores[c].nearest_release)) {
+        if (tick_before(cores[c].nearest_release, sched_ticks)) {
             release(c);
         }
     }
